    "step5_reality_check": {
      "0": "Screenshots show the platform\u2019s Search Results page with a visible \u201cSearch Details\u201d line explicitly stating the query \u201ctype 2 diabetes,\u201d along with a results list underneath. The condition/disease field on the left also contains \u201ctype 2 diabetes\u201d in some views, confirming the intended search term was entered and results loaded.",
      "1": "Across screenshots, \u201cRecruiting\u201d is visibly checked in the Study Status filter, and \u201cUnited States\u201d is visible either in the Location input (with \u201cLocation selected\u201d) or in the Search Details line (\u201cIn United States\u201d). However, Phase 3 is inconsistently evidenced: sometimes the Phase 3 checkbox list is visible but appears unchecked, while another screenshot\u2019s Search Details line shows \u201cPhase: 3\u201d and a \u201cClear Filters (3)\u201d button implying three active filters even though the United States selection is not visible in that same frame. Scoring should rely on what is explicitly visible as active/selected (checked box, Search Details chips/text), not on inferred filters.",
      "2": "None of the provided screenshots visibly display a sort control set to \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d or an on-screen indicator that ordering is \u201cnewest first.\u201d The visible UI elements include view toggles (Card/Table/Map/By Topic) and action buttons (Download/Save/RSS/Display), but no \u201cSort by\u201d dropdown/selection is shown in-frame. Also, the study cards/rows shown do not visibly include \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d values that would allow validating order.",
      "3": "The identity of the first displayed result varies by screenshot (different topmost NCTs appear in different frames), indicating the list view/state changed during the trajectory. Where a specific top result is visible, its NCT, title, and Recruiting badge are readable; however, \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d is not shown on the visible result cards/rows in the screenshots provided, so that required field cannot be captured 'exactly as shown' from these views.",
      "4": "As with result #1, the second displayed study depends on which screenshot state is used (e.g., table vs card view, different points in navigation). In screenshots where the second result is visible, NCT/title/status can be read, but no \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date is visible for that second item in the captured UI portions. Any scoring should account for the absence of the required date field on-screen.",
      "5": "Several screenshots only partially show a third result (card truncated at the bottom) or show only two cards within the captured area, so the full title for #3 is sometimes cut off and the third item may not be fully visible at all. Additionally, no \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date is visible for the third displayed item in the screenshots, even when the NCT number and Recruiting badge are visible.",
      "6": "Screenshots do not show prohibited actions being taken (no evidence of saving, contacting, or submitting information); only passive elements like \u201cSave\u201d buttons and \u201cFind Contact Information\u201d links appear. However, the stopping-condition components requiring visible confirmation of all three filters plus newest-first \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d sorting are not simultaneously visible in most frames, and the required \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d dates are not visible on the result entries shown, which affects whether the task can be considered fully complete based on what the UI actually displayed."
    },
